config ZMK_GESTURE_ACTION
    bool "Enable runtime-configurable gesture actions"
    default y
    depends on DT_HAS_JPTTM_ZMK_BEHAVIOR_GESTURE_ACTION_ENABLED
    depends on SETTINGS
    select ZMK_BEHAVIOR_LOCAL_IDS
    help
      Provides &gesture_action <slot>, a behaviour whose target binding is
      stored in settings and can be changed at runtime. Intended for mouse
      gestures, which would otherwise have to consume runtime macro slots that
      users need for ordinary macros.

      Enabled automatically once a gesture-action node exists in the
      devicetree, so including behaviors/gesture_action.dtsi is all that is
      needed. Without that, the node would compile in with no driver behind it
      and every gesture would silently do nothing.

if ZMK_GESTURE_ACTION

config ZMK_GESTURE_ACTION_STUDIO_RPC
    bool "Expose gesture actions over the custom Studio RPC protocol"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_STUDIO
    help
      Lets a web UI read and reassign gesture actions over USB or Bluetooth.
      Without this the behaviour still works, but every slot is fixed to its
      devicetree default.

config ZMK_GESTURE_ACTION_LAYER_GROUPS
    bool "Expose mouse-gesture layer groups over RPC"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_GESTURE_ACTION_STUDIO_RPC
    depends on ZMK_MOUSE_GESTURE
    help
      Lets the settings UI read and change which layers each mouse-gesture
      processor acts on, so a whole gesture set can be moved from one layer to
      another without a rebuild. Needs kot149/zmk-mouse-gesture with
      active-layers support.

config ZMK_GESTURE_ACTION_COUNT
    int "Number of gesture action slots"
    default 24
    range 1 64
    help
      How many independently assignable actions exist. Each slot costs a
      handful of bytes of RAM and one settings entry, so this can be generous
      compared to runtime macro slots.

      Keep it modest anyway: the slot list is offered as one pickable entry per
      slot, and a Studio UI has to fit them all on screen. DYA Studio's
      key-assignment dialog stops short of about 28 entries with no way to
      scroll to the rest, which strands the tail of a long list.

endif
